# People Recruit — Project Standards

Stack: Next.js, React, Tailwind, Prisma, Supabase PostgreSQL, Vercel.

## 1. Prisma & Database

- Always prefer lean `select` over broad `include` to avoid over-fetching.
- Parallelize independent database queries using `Promise.all`.
- Do NOT modify `prisma/schema.prisma` unless explicitly requested.
- Whenever schema changes or new indexes are requested, always generate a safe, idempotent PostgreSQL script (`CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ...`) ready for Supabase SQL Editor.

## 2. Frontend & UX

- Use `next/dynamic` for heavy client-side components (modals, rich editors, charts).
- Provide skeleton loaders or clean loading states for async data.
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders and full-page refetches on minor mutations (prefer Optimistic UI).

## 3. Deployment & Verification

- Before finishing any task, run `npx tsc --noEmit` (and `npm run build` for major changes) to guarantee Vercel production builds will pass.
- Keep code changes minimal and focused; do not refactor unrelated files or delete existing comments.

## 4. Communication

- Respond concisely in Ukrainian, using bullet points for summaries.
